From: Mano Thanabalan <mano.thanabalan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:59:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hal: declare smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_kick() (lost-edge
 resuscitation)

---
 smtc_rac_lib/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.h | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.h b/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.h
index 524fe9c..d97fc0e 100644
--- a/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.h
+++ b/smtc_rac_lib/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.h
@@ -272,6 +272,19 @@ uint32_t smtc_modem_hal_get_random_nb_in_range( const uint32_t val_1, const uint
  */
 void smtc_modem_hal_irq_config_radio_irq( void ( *callback )( void* context ), void* context );
 
+/**
+ * @brief Re-inject the radio IRQ event into the stack (lost-edge
+ *        resuscitation).
+ *
+ * The transceiver's event pin interrupt is edge-triggered while the chip
+ * holds its IRQ line high until the mask is cleared over SPI. An edge
+ * fired while the GPIO interrupt is momentarily disabled is lost forever.
+ * The application main loop calls this when the pin is observed stuck
+ * high: it invokes the registered radio IRQ callback exactly as the GPIO
+ * ISR would have. Idempotent when no IRQ is actually pending.
+ */
+void smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_kick( void );
+
 /* ------------ Radio management ------------
  *@brief Check if the radio is free
  * @remark except a very specific application, this function should always return false
